    "termsOfUse": "Users interested in the use of DALC for research purposes may obtain the dataset in the standard format and in the full text format. Users can freely download the standard format from the DALC GitHub repository. \n\nResearchers affiliated with universities or not-for-profit research institutes may use the full version of DALC in accordance with the Data Transfer Agreement provided by the University of Groningen. \n\nThe data may be used only for the purpose of conducting not-for-profit scientific research. \n\nIt is not allowed to actively search online for any of the information contained in the full version of DALC. \n\nIt is not allowed to disclose the full version of DALC to any third party or otherwise use it for your own benefit or for the benefit of a third party, without first obtaining written consent from the University of Groningen\n",
    "restrictions": "For reasons of compliance with Twitter/X Terms of Use (March, 2023) and to protect data subjects given the sensitive nature of the data, certain files of DALC are under restricted access.  As such, signing a Data Transfer Agreement provided by the University of Groningen is part of the procedure for re-use of the full version of DALC. \n<br>\n<br>\nThe agreement will enter into force as of the date both parties have signed it. The agreement will continue to be effective during the period that you possess the data. During that period, you cannot terminate the agreement. \n\nThe University of Groningen may terminate the agreement if you have not cured a breach of the agreement within a reasonable period of being notified of such a breach. \n\nAt the request of the University of Groningen, you will return or destroy all copies of the full version of DALC.",
    "termsOfAccess": "Permission for re-use can be granted by the University of Groningen Digital Competence Centre on behalf of the first author after inspecting credentials and the reason for request. The procedure starts with a request for access via this dataset at DataverseNL. \n\nSigning of a Data Transfer Agreement is part of the procedure for re-use of the data. ",
    "contactForAccess": "dcc@rug.nl; \nt.caselli@rug.nl",
